Navigation note: the web route /vehicle-comparison is single-segment, so the first-segment AppRouteParser
resolves it directly via the new route's pathSegment ("vehicle-comparison") — no alias needed (cf. the sibling
FleetTelemetryCoverage which needed a /admin/telemetry/coverage alias because its web path is multi-segment).
A dedicated .fleetCompare route (Insights sidebar group) was added rather than displacing the existing
.analytics route (covenant #7). MenuCommandCatalog.navigateCommands() derives from AppRoute.allCases, so the new
case is auto-covered (testNavigateCommandsCoverEveryRoute stays green); the pathSegment is unique
(testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment stays green); the route resolves to its Insights group
(testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup stays green). The two web CTAs (single-vehicle "Manage vehicles" and the
period-compare banner) navigate through an injected onNavigate shell hook (selection = .vehicles / .analytics),
mirroring SettingsRouteRegistration's onOpenNotifications pattern; the banner dismissal persists in UserDefaults
under the web localStorage key phase40.compareBanner.dismissed.fleet.

